{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod","id":1340250,"title":"Comprehensive list of Realms in CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-08T09:57:34-07:00","id":1340250,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Comprehensive list of Realms in CoD","content":"Is there a list anywhere that someone has compiled of a list of Realms and the various denizens that are native to them?<br /> <br /> Here's what I have so far but I'm new to CoD so I'm sure I don't know all of them.<br /> <br /> Astral - Goetia / Primordial Dream (as part of the Astral Plane) - Beasts<br /> Shadow - Spirits<br /> Underworld - Ghosts<br /> Twilight - Not a realm per se<br /> Hedge - Changelings/Hobgoblins<br /> Arcadia - True Fae/Huntsmen<br /> Abyss - Demons (from MtA)?<br /> Supernal - ?<br /> <br /> Duat - Mummies<br /> <br /> EDIT 1: Looking at the Fandom page for Supernal Realms located <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Supernal_Realm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, there are a bunch more.<br /> EDIT 2,3 and 4: Adding more content based on the posted below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","user":"Ghostdriver","date":". 10-15-2019, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T10:17:33-07:00","id":1340255,"title":"","content":"Twilight isn't a realm, it is a term to describe the state of Ephemera in certain realms. Not everything in a state of Twilight can see/interact with everything else in a state of Twilight. They generally need to be made of/charged with the same sort of stuff/energy to see each other.<br /> <br /> Not all realms support states of Twilight; in realms that don't support Twilight, everything can interact with everything else.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also:<br /> The natives of the Astral are Goetia.<br /> True Fae and Huntsmen come from Faerie/Arcadia which isn't the same as The Hedge.<br /> The Supernal is home to a bunch of different things that can be summoned.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Changelings aren't from any one realm exactly; they were humans from the material world, but being dragged through The Hedge and residing in Arcadia are both critical parts of becoming Changelings.<br /> <br /> EDIT 3: I'm pretty sure the term for the creatures from The Hedge is Hobgoblin, I'm pretty sure &quot;Goblin&quot; is used to refer to any Fae related thing that is particularly tricky. Goblin fruit aren't simply any food from The Hedge they have weird (pun intended) effects. Goblin Markets will scam you out of everything you own if you aren't careful. Changelings can become Goblins (and even Goblin Queens) if they take on too much Goblin Debt but they are still Changelings not Hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-08-2019, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T12:14:10-07:00","id":1340275,"title":"","content":"Ghosts are technically not &quot;native&quot; to the Underworld. They generate in the material realm (or wherever it is they died), and the Underworld exerts a pull on deathly things that eventually pulls ghosts in. There are ghostly beings called chthonians which do appear to be native to the Underworld itself.<br /> <br /> As Custos says, Twilight is not a realm. It's the state of being ephemeral or immaterial. Different &quot;phases&quot; of Twilight are sometimes referenced to reflect how, for example, Twilit ghosts can't see or touch Twilit spirits or Twilit angels.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins and Hedge ghosts (which are not &quot;ghosts&quot; proper) are native to the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking, there are indications the True Fae may not be &quot;native&quot; to Faerie, though Faerie is certainly where those who are known dwell and have power. If they did not come from Faerie but somewhere else, it is not known what or where that somewhere else is.<br /> <br /> The Abyss's native entities are, well, Abyssal entities. Those which intrude into reality divide into acamoth, which resemble goetia, gulmoth, which resemble spirits, and the touch of the cosmic-scale Annunaki. It may or may not be useful to describe the Abyss as a &quot;realm,&quot; because if it is possible to go there without being destroyed by the experience, no one seems to have come back to prove it.<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths are an entire category of many different realms of existence in Mage which lack some essential element of being. Again, many of these are not very useful to describe as &quot;realms,&quot; because you can't very well explore the non-place where the concept of space doesn't exist. Mages call beings native to Lower Realms able to support their existence &quot;akathartoi,&quot; though this too is an umbrella term for what are likely thousands of distinct types of beings.<br /> <br /> The Supernal Realm is the world of concepts, symbols and meaning, as viewed separately from the world of phenomenon and form which those symbols assume. Mages experience one of five Supernal Realms (or rather five faces of the one Supernal Realm, each face manifest as its own symbol-world) depending on their Path of Awakening, and give different names to the supernal symbol-gods reflected in each of those five Realms, one named type of being for each of the ten supernal Arcana.<br /> <br /> The Duat is a mysterious realm somehow connected to mummies and their Rite of Return, which they travel between lives. It is host to the cosmic Judges of Life and Death, as well as to lesser beings which are referred to as &quot;demons,&quot; but which are unrelated to any other type of demon.<br /> <br /> Many various other realms of existence have been referenced in different books which are likely separate from all of these, such as the Other City which manifests in Glasgow, and the interstitial terrains glimpsed in the Horror Recognition Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T14:59:44-07:00","id":1340305,"title":"","content":"In the Demon's Storytellers Guide, page 84 - Delivery: This Incept also allows the angel to<i> spend Essence equal to the local Gauntlet</i> to <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>create a portal to any other ephemeral realm, from the Underworld to the Astral Realms to the Abyss</b></span>.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that an Angel from DtD can travel to all the realms listed above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T15:15:47-07:00","id":1340307,"title":"","content":"Traditionally portals don't guarantee survival at their destination. Can travel, sure. Can live there, depends on whoever's going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T15:46:56-07:00","id":1340312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1340307#post1340307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally portals don't guarantee survival at their destination. Can travel, sure. Can live there, depends on whoever's going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, they're often necessary for summoning methods to be able to actually work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T16:21:58-07:00","id":1340316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1340275#post1340275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Duat is a mysterious realm somehow connected to mummies and their Rite of Return, which they travel between lives. It is host to the cosmic Judges of Life and Death, as well as to lesser beings which are referred to as &quot;demons,&quot; but which are unrelated to any other type of demon.<br /> <br /> Many various other realms of existence have been referenced in different books which are likely separate from all of these, such as the Other City which manifests in Glasgow, and the interstitial terrains glimpsed in the Horror Recognition Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely recall seeing somewhere that some Mages are aware of Duat and consider it a Lower Depth. If that's the case, many Mages would likely label most unusual realms they encounter a Lower Depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T16:41:52-07:00","id":1340322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1340316#post1340316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vaguely recall seeing somewhere that some Mages are aware of Duat and consider it a Lower Depth. If that's the case, many Mages would likely label most unusual realms they encounter a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. Only the ones that consume the Fallen Worlds. Like, you know, Duat does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T17:07:30-07:00","id":1341346,"title":"","content":"The catch all term for beings from the Supernal Realm is Supernal Beings (though each have other names as well).<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is a part of the Astral Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T06:40:45-07:00","id":1341431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1341346#post1341346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The catch all term for beings from the Supernal Realm is Supernal Beings (though each have other names as well).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which book(s) would be best to read up on 'Supernal Beings'? I'd like to know more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T06:53:54-07:00","id":1341433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostdriver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1341431#post1341431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book(s) would be best to read up on 'Supernal Beings'? I'd like to know more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big one is <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/60624/Summoners\" target=\"_blank\">Summoners</a>, which has a whole chapter dedicated to their summoning and use. Much of the systems from there found their way into Mage 2e Core, but Summoners has a bit more room to unpack examples and description by virtue of not having quite as stringent a wordcount premium to fit the subject into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T08:46:39-07:00","id":1341446,"title":"","content":"You could start listing the Lower Depths, as they are indeed a collection of many, hungry realms. Inferno, Duat, Annwn and wherever the strix come from, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T11:19:56-07:00","id":1341477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1341446#post1341446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could start listing the Lower Depths, as they are indeed a collection of many, hungry realms. Inferno, Duat, Annwn and wherever the strix come from, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; referenced in a book somewhere? I'd love to read up on that too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T11:29:34-07:00","id":1341481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostdriver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340250-comprehensive-list-of-realms-in-cod?p=1341477#post1341477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; referenced in a book somewhere? I'd love to read up on that too!</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly in Mage, even though there isn't some full description of all of those realms. I think that summoners present a number of such Depths, while Imperial Mysteries and Left Handed Path further cement and develop the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}